cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the MICROMar Atlas in scientific papers, reports, presentations, or other academic outputs, please cite this software."
title: "MICROMar Atlas: Interactive Atlas of Microplastic Pollution in Brazilian Coastal Sediments"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"

authors:
  - family-names: "Marinho da Luz"
    given-names: "Thiarlen"
  - family-names: "Malafaia"
    given-names: "Guilherme"

identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23045182"

repository-code: "https://github.com/thiarleneluzifgoiano/micromar-atlas"
url: "https://thiarleneluzifgoiano.github.io/micromar-atlas/"

abstract: >-
  MICROMar Atlas is an interactive platform for visualizing, exploring, and
  comparing data on microplastic pollution in Brazilian coastal sediments.
  Version 1.0.0 brings together information from 4,134 georeferenced samples,
  1,024 beaches, 211 municipalities, and 17 coastal states, integrating spatial
  distribution, microplastic composition, pollution load indicators, polymer
  hazard, ecological risk, and environmental factors.

keywords:
  - microplastics
  - coastal sediments
  - Brazil
  - pollution
  - ecological risk
  - data visualization
  - MICROMar
